Scratch detector used by Photographic Studio By Bill (Develop > Old photo and film > Remove dust and scratches)

scratch_detector.npz    the scratch-detection U-Net of "Bringing Old Photos Back to Life"

Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation. Licensed under the MIT License; the licence text is in the file LICENSE in this
folder. Source: https://github.com/microsoft/Bringing-Old-Photos-Back-to-Life (release v1.0,
global_checkpoints.zip, checkpoints/detection/FT_Epoch_latest.pt). The repository states that its code and
pretrained models are under the MIT licence.

Paper: Ziyu Wan, Bo Zhang, Dongdong Chen, Pan Zhang, Dong Chen, Jing Liao, Fang Wen, "Bringing Old Photos Back to
Life", CVPR 2020, and "Old Photo Restoration via Deep Latent Space Translation", IEEE TPAMI 2022.

What was changed: only the model's own weights were kept (not the optimiser state saved with them); each
convolution's batch normalisation was folded into its weights; the weights are stored as 8-bit integers with one
scale per filter. tools/convert_scratch_detector.py does all of it, without PyTorch, from Microsoft's file. The
network is run by the Studio's own NumPy code (studio/engine/local/scratchnet.py, GPL-3.0); PyTorch is not used.
